ed to start by actually going to  those places going to those prisoner of  war camps  president steinmeier himself was foreign  minister before he became president and  in that position  he was for example he was the first  german politician to actually  commemorate the victims in belarus  on a trip there um to the biggest  concentration camp  during soviet occupation that is uh  located near minsk and that history  completely risked to be forgotten so  steinmeier  kept going to those places he went to  volgograd as well where he met with war  veterans  and germany politicians are now saying  in their speeches  that it was part of the nazi's official  plan to kill the population  in the east and get rid of entire  nations that way  uw's political correspondent nina hazard  there thank you nina  you
 

